# Custom domain — instructions
#
# Currently using the default GitHub Pages URL: jackcampbell5.github.io
# No CNAME record is needed for that.
#
# To point a custom domain here later:
#   1. Replace everything in this file with just your domain, e.g.:
#        jackcamp.dev
#   2. In your DNS provider, add a CNAME record:
#        Name: www (or @)  →  Value: jackcampbell5.github.io
#      For an apex domain (@), use four A records pointing to GitHub's IPs instead:
#        185.199.108.153
#        185.199.109.153
#        185.199.110.153
#        185.199.111.153
#   3. In GitHub repo Settings → Pages, set your custom domain.
#   4. GitHub will auto-provision an SSL certificate within a few minutes.
#
# Leave this file in place even without a custom domain — GitHub Pages expects it.
